  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>gemcitabine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L01BC05</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, IV dosing <small>(PK_2C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Serdjebi C et al. 2017</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>adults with pancreatic cancer</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>gemcitabine</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_gemcitabine/Gemcitabine_Serdjebi2017_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>V1</td><td>45</td><td>L</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>CL1</td><td>4.03</td><td>L/min</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>V2</td><td>36</td><td>L</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr><tr><td>CL2</td><td>0.226</td><td>L/min</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr></table><h4>About gemcitabine</h4><p>Gemcitabine is an antimetabolite anticancer drug used to treat various cancers, including pancreatic, lung, bladder, and breast-related carcinomas as well as several lymphomas. It is an approved medicine and is included on the WHO list of essential medicines, so it is widely used in cancer treatment worldwide.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q414143\">Wikidata Q414143</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Gemcitabine\">Gemcitabine</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Serdjebi C et al. (2017). Population Pharmacokinetics of Gemcitabine and dFdU in Pancreatic Cancer Patients Using an Optimal Design, Sparse Sampling Approach. <i>Therapeutic drug monitoring 39(3):290–296</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://